<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its February 13 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.45 (13.49)	     13.92 (13.96)</p>
<p>    Six months	    13.73 (13.94)	     14.74 (14.98)</p>
<p>    12 months	     13.30 (13.33)	     15.33 (15.37)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 16.30 (16.34)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307  745308</p>
